Z||000000||1FieroGTRacingInc||09-07-2000||07:37 AM||||what causes my GT to jerk or surge when driving a steady speed(55)???  thanks steve||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||09-07-2000||08:35 AM||||Does it only do it at a steady 55 mph or does it do it throughout the rpm range?  Mine started acting up (very pronounced jerking) and it turned out to be the ECM going out.  New ECM and all is better.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||09-07-2000||01:05 PM||||FWIW, my 1986 SE V-6 used to shudder/miss at highway speed.  Didn't do it all the time, so I let it go for months.  Finally (by luck), found out it was a plug wire that wouldn't stay tightly on the plug.<P>Carrolles, how did you find out it was the ECM?  Is there a good way to isolate it, other than guess and try?    ||||reg||5
Z||000003||loafer87gt||09-07-2000||01:34 PM||||I had a similar problem with my 87GT and the culprit turned out to be the tach filter. Try unplugging it and see if that solves the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ROB MAC||09-07-2000||03:44 PM||||Mine would do it at accelleration and while driving just as you let up on the gas pedal. It was the O2 sensor.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||09-07-2000||04:57 PM||||StuGood,<P>I followed the diagnostic fault tree in the Helms manual.  I ran out of time due to out of town work assignment and finally took it to the dealer.  He found the problem.||||reg||1
